# Scenario: one end-to-end HTTP/2 round trip over the nghttp2-driven arm
# H2-2 adds, and the worker-inside evidence that makes it admissible.
#
# WHAT MAKES THIS ADMISSIBLE, stated first because it is the only question
# worth asking of a new scenario here (H2-1's alpn-negotiation.rule opens the
# same way, and this file inherits the argument). "The prober can speak h2"
# is not a finding on its own: it proves nginx does what nginx does, and
# Test::Nginx::Socket's HTTP/2 support (where it exists) can already reach a
# listener configured for it. What makes this row admissible is the same
# thing that made H2-1's: the `delta` assertion below is evidence that came
# from INSIDE the worker, not from the client's own observation that the
# exchange completed. A client watching the wire cannot tell "the worker
# served this h2 request and gave back every descriptor it used" apart from
# "the worker leaked one and got lucky this run" -- the probe snapshot is the
# only place that distinction is visible.
#
# THE TEST THAT KEEPS THIS HONEST: remove the probe snapshot below and the
# case still reports a pass on the exact same server behaviour a descriptor
# leak would also produce, because nothing else here asserts on the module's
# internal state. That is the wrong-oracle failure this file is built not to
# have.
#
# WHAT THIS ROW IS NOT. H2-2's own scope, restated from the TODO row: this is
# the MECHANISM plus one clean round trip, not an attack. The case below sends
# a well-formed request over a well-formed h2 connection and expects the
# well-formed response any h2 client would get. Hostile h2 framing (oversized
# HEADERS, HPACK attacks, stream-lifecycle abuse) is H2-3/H2-4/H2-5's job, not
# this file's -- adding one here would be scope creep against the row this
# file exists to close.

name          a well-formed h2 request round-trips end to end
send          GET / HTTP/1.1\r\n
send          Host: prober\r\nConnection: close\r\n\r\n
alpn           h2
expect_alpn    h2
expect         status=200
expect         body~OK
delta          fds == 0
probe_baseline fds == 0
